  "summary": "Flock Safety confirmed it mistakenly removed six license plate reader cameras in Lebanon, Ohio, after they had been covered and flagged as inactive during a city council-ordered pause. The council recently voted 4-3 against terminating the Flock contract while continuing to review the agreement amid community concerns over transparency and data retention.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The cameras were removed in error, and Flock is working with the customer to determine the appropriate next steps,",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "Lebanon City Council voted 4-3 earlier this month against terminating its contract with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "The cameras had been covered with bags since September, when Lebanon City Council voted to pause the program after Flock failed to meet the mayor's deadline to respond to a series of questions about the company's data practices.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    }
  ],
